{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage","id":1515850,"title":"Healing aggravated damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-22T05:29:22-07:00","id":1515850,"title":"Healing aggravated damage","content":"Hello guys, how healing aggravated damage works?<br /> <br /> Let's say, you are a blood potency 1 vampire, and you take 2 aggravated damage. So to heal that you need 10 vitae and a full day sleep. Until here I got it. But...<ul><li>The vitae spent is sleeping or before?</li> <li>The full day sleep is 24 hours sleeping or just during the day as usual?</li> </ul>The thing is, if the vitae is spent during the sleep the vampire will go in torpor without blood to awake, and the healing will trigger anyway because of cleansing (unless you spend willpower). Nothing says your can't spend before sleep, and feed to have blood to awake, but I'm not sure if that's how is intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","user":"ImortalKiller","date":".  Fixing typos 06-22-2023, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T06:02:20-07:00","id":1515854,"title":"","content":"You need five Vitae and a full day's sleep for a single aggravated wound, so if you don't spend the five Vitae beforehand and/or spend Willpower to stop it from automatically being deducted you lose it during your next daysleep and need to sleep the full dawn-to-dusk period to heal the one point of damage, and then this repeats the next day.<br /> <br /> Assuming the mechanic isn't meant to differ too significantly from 1e, you can spend Vitae toward healing aggravated damage over the course of a night; the requirement of sleeping a full day in 2e replaces the 1e timing of aggravated healing needing the expenditure to be done over the course of two nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T06:19:27-07:00","id":1515857,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see it. Thank you for your help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:01:45-07:00","id":1517894,"title":"","content":"I read, somewhere, that Agg. damage can cause scars on vampires, which, I don't like. If you imagine just how long a vampire can, &quot;Live&quot;, and just how often Agg.-damage comes up, there's a possibility that, after a century a vampire could look like a Nos. with all the scars they've, &quot;Collected&quot;: yeah, story-hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:32:19-07:00","id":1517899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage?p=1517894#post1517894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read, somewhere, that Agg. damage can cause scars on vampires, which, I don't like. If you imagine just how long a vampire can, &quot;Live&quot;, and just how often Agg.-damage comes up, there's a possibility that, after a century a vampire could look like a Nos. with all the scars they've, &quot;Collected&quot;: yeah, story-hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunlight doesn't start causing aggravated damage until Humanity 4, aggravated damage from fire can be downgraded to lethal with Resilience, and not having any natural healing is incentive enough for vampires to avoid damage in general and aggravated damage in particular. If you're getting into enough trouble to take that many aggravated wounds as a vampire you do not have your Requiem put together well, and if explicitly normal-looking scarring (the bit you're remembering is from the section on Healing on page 91 of the corebook) is enough to equate to being supernaturally unsettling to talk to you have worse problems than scarring to worry about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T23:36:21-07:00","id":1517921,"title":"","content":"Not to mention you say &quot;just how often aggravated damage comes up&quot; as if that is &quot;pretty often,&quot; and that hasn't been my experience with Requiem. Sunlight isn't hard to avoid if you secure your haven, fire is hard for your enemies to use as a weapon in the middle of a city without going to careful pains or attracting unwanted attention, damaging banes afflicting your Humanity can be kept secret, and other sources of aggravated damage are pretty rare.<br /> <br /> First edition, where three dots in Protean gave you an aggravated natural weapon, your mileage may vary. Second edition raises the investment cost on supernatural aggravated assault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:41:58-07:00","id":1518383,"title":"","content":"Personally, I quite like aggravated giving a scar. Let's say you got into a fight with a werewolf, and got a scar you couldn't completely heal and you can't really explain to mortals close to you how you got and how healed so fast a injury which make that big scar. Besides, could even become a physical reminder to the character of a traumatic experience... or just a &quot;don't mess with werewolves&quot;. <br /> <br /> Werewolves aside, I don't think overall this should be a concern, kindred downgrade aggravated to lethal (of course, except banes) unless is something which was spent resources upon (or implies that should) . So basically you should be getting aggravated damage in memorable fights against powerful enemies which can deal directly aggravated with impressive displays of power, or can roll lethal to aggravated. Both situations your enemy must be really numerous or formidable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T06:59:51-07:00","id":1518637,"title":"","content":"It heals during daysleep as others have pointed out assuming you have the vitae, I always rolled that if you heal it the night you get it during that day sleep you receive no scar. There are some devotions that counter this and allow you to heal it outside of daysleep.<br /> <br /> The elder level power from the newer Gangrel clan book has a devotion called Regeneration that allows aggravated wounds to be healed but it requires protean 4 and resilience 4, it cost 5 vitae per wound and causes a condition that persists for scenes equal to wounds healed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T20:50:32-07:00","id":1518804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage?p=1518383#post1518383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I quite like aggravated giving a scar. Let's say you got into a fight with a werewolf, and got a scar you couldn't completely heal and you can't really explain to mortals close to you how you got and how healed so fast a injury which make that big scar. Besides, could even become a physical reminder to the character of a traumatic experience... or just a &quot;don't mess with werewolves&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aside, I don't think overall this should be a concern, kindred downgrade aggravated to lethal (of course, except banes) unless is something which was spent resources upon (or implies that should) . So basically you should be getting aggravated damage in memorable fights against powerful enemies which can deal directly aggravated with impressive displays of power, or can roll lethal to aggravated. Both situations your enemy must be really numerous or formidable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea of the ageless and timeless, &quot;Vampire&quot;, that always returns to their state of undeath, as they died, but, Agg.-Dmg. from sunlight and fires, does leave a scar, but those go away, in time. However, the claws causing Agg.-Dmg., from another supernatural-being, say, a werewolf, well, that's a different-story. <br /> <br /> In my games, thanks to a werewolf's spiffy-healing, they don't age either. But the older they get, the more scars they have. They don't get gray-hair, or wrinkles, as the body heals, but, agg.-dmg., leaves a mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T21:21:48-07:00","id":1518808,"title":"","content":"Werewolf claws don't cause aggravated. I don't think they even cause lethal to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T05:15:37-07:00","id":1518819,"title":"","content":"Exactly, in 2ed very few things causes agg damages. Werewolves' claws only causes bashing, while bite causes lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T17:52:50-07:00","id":1518975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage?p=1517899#post1517899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunlight doesn't start causing aggravated damage until Humanity 4, aggravated damage from fire can be downgraded to lethal with Resilience, and not having any natural healing is incentive enough for vampires to avoid damage in general and aggravated damage in particular. If you're getting into enough trouble to take that many aggravated wounds as a vampire you do not have your Requiem put together well, and if explicitly normal-looking scarring (the bit you're remembering is from the section on Healing on page 91 of the corebook) is enough to equate to being supernaturally unsettling to talk to you have worse problems than scarring to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is more with rollover agg. It can be cool if your character barely escaped a mob with torches and has the burn scar to remind them of it, but if your character gets into a scrap and after a few cuts and scrapes ends up taking a hit from a lead pipe that rolls over into agg damage, it seems a bit silly for that to leave a permanent mark. It's not narratively interesting, and trying to come up with exactly what/where the scar would be can be a challenge in and of itself. Our group ignores scarring from rollover agg for this reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T20:47:54-07:00","id":1518988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage?p=1518975#post1518975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue is more with rollover agg. It can be cool if your character barely escaped a mob with torches and has the burn scar to remind them of it, but if your character gets into a scrap and after a few cuts and scrapes ends up taking a hit from a lead pipe that rolls over into agg damage, it seems a bit silly for that to leave a permanent mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lead pipe is going to do bashing damage to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Even if it didn't, enough existing bashing damage to cause lethal to roll over into agg is substantially more than &quot;a few cuts and scrapes,&quot; because lethal damage doesn't upgrade bashing to agg. The later presentation of the mechanics in post-Changeling 2e lines is more explicit about it, but even in Requiem 2e core the wording is that taking lethal with a full track of bashing just turns the existing bashing damage into lethal damage; the newer presentation just makes it explicit that more severe wounds push lesser wounds toward the end of the Health track but never cause them to &quot;overflow&quot; the gauge.<br /> <br /> If you have 7 Health and take 4 bashing damage followed by 4 lethal damage, you have 4 lethal wounds and 3 bashing wounds, not 5 lethal and 2 bashing from one of the bashing boxes not fitting into the available boxes. Taking minimally successful hits with a tire iron, a vampire with 7 Health needs to be struck eight times before they start taking aggravated damage, and that's assuming they don't spend any Vitae on healing or Resilience. Accumulating damage over a longer period of time is likewise unlikely because of the way the daysleep makes holding off on healing a directed effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T21:45:52-07:00","id":1518991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage?p=1518988#post1518988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lead pipe is going to do bashing damage to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Even if it didn't, enough existing bashing damage to cause lethal to roll over into agg is substantially more than &quot;a few cuts and scrapes,&quot; because lethal damage doesn't upgrade bashing to agg. The later presentation of the mechanics in post-Changeling 2e lines is more explicit about it, but even in Requiem 2e core the wording is that taking lethal with a full track of bashing just turns the existing bashing damage into lethal damage; the newer presentation just makes it explicit that more severe wounds push lesser wounds toward the end of the Health track but never cause them to &quot;overflow&quot; the gauge.<br /> <br /> If you have 7 Health and take 4 bashing damage followed by 4 lethal damage, you have 4 lethal wounds and 3 bashing wounds, not 5 lethal and 2 bashing from one of the bashing boxes not fitting into the available boxes. Taking minimally successful hits with a tire iron, a vampire with 7 Health needs to be struck eight times before they start taking aggravated damage, and that's assuming they don't spend any Vitae on healing or Resilience. Accumulating damage over a longer period of time is likewise unlikely because of the way the daysleep makes holding off on healing a directed effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know how the system works, thanks.<br /> <br /> It doesn't change the fact that you can be on 5 lethal, 2 bashing and take a punch for 4 bashing. Now you have 2 points of agg. It's hard to see how that translates to a permanent scar in a way that's satisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T22:08:28-07:00","id":1518993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1515850-healing-aggravated-damage?p=1518991#post1518991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't change the fact that you can be on 5 lethal, 2 bashing and take a punch for 4 bashing. Now you have 2 points of agg. It's hard to see how that translates to a permanent scar in a way that's satisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are taking four points of damage from a punch on top of having sustained nearly a full track of lethal you are having a <i>bad fucking night</i> even setting aside the bigger issue that you're literally getting beaten into torpor by that hit.<br /> <br /> If a vampire is sticking around long past the point where getting gone was a prudent decision and they suffer a blow of any intensity that functionally kills them in that situation, you have a solid rationale for that character to have a reminder of the time they were rendered as close to dead as a vampire can be and still survive.<br /> <br /> It's a storytelling game. Broken noses and rough patches of skin and unpleasant discoloration can serve as mementos of those points in the Kindred's life where the pristine state restored by the Cleansing is marred by the indignity of defeat. Your group is welcome to their opinions, but &quot;I got beaten nearly to death and the blow that knocked me into a years-long coma or forced me a step closer to servitude left a lasting mark&quot; seems anything but silly to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}